# 🧭 Component Taxonomy Report — CodeMind Playbook

> **Purpose:** Automatically analyze any repository and produce a rich, structured Component Taxonomy Report — covering architectural classification, technology profile, responsibility mapping, health signals, and actionable recommendations. No hardcoding; every inference is derived dynamically from the repository contents.

---

## 📋 Playbook Metadata

```yaml
playbook_id:       component-taxonomy-report
playbook_version:  1.0.0
target_tool:       CodeMind IDE
report_type:       Component Taxonomy & Architectural Classification
applicable_to:     Any software repository (microservice, library, monolith, batch job, UI app, data pipeline, etc.)
generated_by:      CodeMind AI Agent
```

---

## 🎯 What This Report Produces

A **Component Taxonomy Report** classifies a repository along key architectural dimensions and produces:

| Section | What It Answers |
|---|---|
| **Identity** | What is this component? Who owns it? |
| **Taxonomy** | Category → Sub-Category → Type classification |
| **Tech Profile** | Languages, frameworks, runtime, build tooling |
| **Responsibility Map** | What does it do? What does it NOT do? |
| **Integration Topology** | How does it connect to the outside world? |
| **Deployment Fingerprint** | How and where does it run? |
| **Code Quality Signals** | What does the code itself reveal about maturity? |
| **Risk & Gap Analysis** | What's missing or concerning? |
| **Recommendations** | Concrete next steps |

