## 🏷️ Phase 2 — Taxonomy Classification

> Apply the following decision trees to assign the three-level taxonomy: Category → Sub-Category → Type.

### 2.1 — Category Classification

```
CATEGORY DECISION TREE:

  IF built and maintained entirely in-house with no COTS license files,
     no vendor SDK jars, and no proprietary framework indicators
  → Category: CUSTOM

  ELSE IF primary codebase is a vendor product being configured/extended
     (e.g., Salesforce config, ServiceNow customization, SAP extensions)
  → Category: COMMERCIAL-OFF-THE-SHELF (COTS)

  ELSE IF a mix of in-house code wrapping a licensed SDK or platform
  → Category: HYBRID

  ELSE IF purely configuration/deployment of an open-source product
     with no custom application code
  → Category: OPEN-SOURCE-DEPLOYMENT

  Document ALL signals used for this decision in the report.
```

---

### 2.2 — Sub-Category Classification

```
SUB-CATEGORY DECISION TREE:

  Web Application / Service:
    - REST controller annotations present (@RestController, @GetMapping, router.get(), etc.)
    - HTTP server framework in dependencies (spring-web, express, fastapi, gin)
    - Exposes HTTP endpoints

  Messaging / Event-Driven Service:
    - Kafka/RabbitMQ/SQS consumer/producer code present
    - No HTTP controller code (or HTTP is secondary)
    - Message listener annotations (@KafkaListener, @RabbitListener, @SqsListener)

  Batch / Scheduled Processing:
    - Job scheduler present (Spring Batch, Quartz, Airflow, Celery Beat)
    - @Scheduled / cron / timer annotations dominant
    - No HTTP or messaging consumer as primary interface

  Data Pipeline / ETL:
    - Extract-Transform-Load pattern present in code
    - Data ingestion, transformation, and sink components present
    - Pipeline orchestration files present (Airflow DAGs, Prefect flows)

  UI / Frontend Application:
    - Frontend framework dependencies present (React, Angular, Vue, etc.)
    - Public assets directory (public/, static/, assets/)
    - HTML entry point (index.html)
    - Build tool (webpack, vite, parcel, esbuild)

  Library / SDK:
    - No main application entry point
    - Exported interfaces/classes designed for external consumption
    - No Dockerfile or deployment manifests
    - Published to artifact registry (Maven Central, npm, PyPI)

  CLI Tool:
    - main() entry point with argument parsing (argparse, cobra, commander, picocli)
    - No server startup code
    - No persistent deployment manifests

  Infrastructure / Platform Component:
    - Primarily IaC files (Terraform, CDK, Helm chart-only repo)
    - No application source code
```

---

### 2.3 — Type Classification

```
TYPE DECISION TREE:

  Microservice:
    - Single focused responsibility (validate, transform, notify, etc.)
    - Own deployment unit (Dockerfile + K8s manifests)
    - Communicates via REST or messaging APIs
    - Stateless (no local database, no shared filesystem)
    - No UI

  Monolith:
    - Multiple distinct domains in one deployment unit
    - Shared database accessed from multiple layers
    - Contains both business logic AND persistence AND (possibly) UI

  Monorepo / Multi-Module:
    - Multiple sub-projects under one root
    - Shared build tooling across modules
    - Each module may be independently deployable

  Sidecar:
    - Injected alongside a primary container
    - Handles cross-cutting concern (logging, proxy, auth)

  Serverless Function:
    - Single-purpose handler function
    - Invoked by trigger (HTTP, event, schedule)
    - No persistent server process

  Gateway / Proxy:
    - Routes, aggregates, or transforms requests
    - Contains routing rules, filters, rate limiting logic
    - No direct business logic

  Worker / Consumer:
    - Subscribes to queue/topic
    - Processes messages asynchronously
    - Persists results or triggers downstream actions
```

