## 🔗 Phase 4 — Integration Topology

> Map all inbound and outbound integration points.

```
INBOUND SIGNALS (how this component is called):
  - HTTP endpoint paths (scan @*Mapping annotations, router definitions, OpenAPI spec)
  - Port numbers (application.properties, server.port, Dockerfile EXPOSE)
  - Queue/topic subscriptions (@KafkaListener topics, @RabbitListener queues)
  - Triggered by: Scheduled cron, event bridge, pubsub subscription

OUTBOUND SIGNALS (what this component calls):
  - HTTP client config (RestTemplate, WebClient, Axios, fetch, requests, httpx)
  - Service URLs in config (application.yaml, .env, config maps)
  - Database connection strings (datasource.url, DATABASE_URL, DB_HOST)
  - Kafka producer topics
  - Cache connections (redis.host, REDIS_URL)
  - External SDK calls (AWS, Azure, GCP SDKs)

OUTPUT FORMAT FOR REPORT:
  Inbound:
    - [PROTOCOL] [PATH/TOPIC] → [PURPOSE]

  Outbound:
    - [PROTOCOL] [TARGET/URL-PATTERN] → [PURPOSE]
```

