## ⚕️ Phase 5 — Code Quality & Maturity Signals

> Assess quality indicators without executing the code.

```
QUALITY SIGNAL MATRIX:

  Testing Coverage Signals:
    ✅ Test directory present (src/test, tests/, __tests__, spec/)
    ✅ Test files present (*.test.*, *Spec.*, *Test.java)
    ✅ Mocking frameworks in dependencies (Mockito, Jest, pytest-mock)
    ✅ Integration test directory separate from unit tests
    ⚠️  No test directory found
    ⚠️  Test files present but test count < 20% of source file count

  Documentation Signals:
    ✅ README.md present and > 200 words
    ✅ API docs (Swagger/OpenAPI spec present)
    ✅ CHANGELOG.md or HISTORY.md present
    ✅ Javadoc / docstrings on public methods > 50%
    ⚠️  README.md absent or < 50 words
    ⚠️  No API documentation found

  Security Signals:
    ✅ Security dependency present (Spring Security, Passport, PyJWT)
    ✅ Secrets not hardcoded (no API keys in source files)
    ✅ Dependency audit config present (OWASP plugin, npm audit, Snyk)
    ⚠️  Secrets detected in source files (flag without exposing values)
    ⚠️  No security dependency detected for an externally-exposed service

  Observability Signals:
    ✅ Structured logging configured
    ✅ Metrics endpoint (Actuator, Prometheus /metrics)
    ✅ Health check endpoint present
    ✅ Distributed tracing dependency (OpenTelemetry, Sleuth, Jaeger)
    ⚠️  No health endpoint detected
    ⚠️  No metrics instrumentation found

  Dependency Hygiene:
    - Count of direct dependencies
    - Count of outdated/flagged dependency versions (if lockfile present)
    - Presence of SBOM (Software Bill of Materials)

  Code Structure:
    - Separation of concerns (Controller → Service → Repository pattern, or equivalent)
    - Presence of dependency injection vs static/singleton abuse
    - Configuration externalized vs hardcoded (check for literal IPs, hardcoded URLs)
```

