## ⚠️ Phase 6 — Risk & Gap Analysis

> Surface gaps between what the component is and what it should have.

```
RISK ASSESSMENT RULES:

  For each taxonomy Type, apply expected standards and flag gaps:

  Microservice risks:
    - MISSING: Health endpoint (required for K8s liveness/readiness probes)
    - MISSING: Structured/JSON logging (required for log aggregation)
    - MISSING: Graceful shutdown handling
    - MISSING: Circuit breaker / retry logic for downstream calls
    - MISSING: Externalized config (no hardcoded URLs, credentials)
    - MISSING: Distributed tracing

  Library risks:
    - MISSING: Published artifact configuration (no pom.xml distributionManagement)
    - MISSING: Semantic versioning enforcement
    - MISSING: Public API documentation
    - MISSING: Backward compatibility strategy

  Batch job risks:
    - MISSING: Job restart/resume logic
    - MISSING: Dead-letter / failure handling
    - MISSING: Run history / audit trail

  ALL types:
    - NO_TESTS: No test directory or zero test files found
    - NO_DOCS: No README.md or empty README
    - SECRETS_IN_CODE: Credential patterns detected in source
    - LARGE_FILES: Files > 500 lines (complexity risk)
    - NO_CI: No CI/CD configuration found
```

